  "solution": {
    "text": "Hydroboration - oxidation reaction of alkenes leads to anti-Markovnikov's hydration. Further addition of water adds in syn-manner, i.e., H and OH are added to the same face of the double bond leading to formation of trans-product. In short, hydroboration-oxidation of alkenes is regioselective as well as stereoselective.",
